  "description": "Upsert support for EF Core: insert a row, or update it if it already exists, in a single database command.\n\nEF Core has no built-in way to do this. The usual workaround is to query first and then insert or update, which costs\nan extra round trip and breaks down when two requests race each other. This library generates the native upsert\nstatement for your database instead, so the check and the write happen atomically.",
  "id": "FlexLabs.EntityFrameworkCore.Upsert",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-11-15T22:35:02.397Z",
